<title>NETHERLANDS: More than half Dutch sugar beet crop planted -- IRS.</title>
<headline>More than half Dutch sugar beet crop planted -- IRS.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Around 60 percent of the 1997 Dutch sugar beet crop has been planted, a figure which should rise to nearer 80 percent by the end of the week, the Institute for Sugar Research (IRS) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The planting is going well and the weather is favourable for the crop,&quot; IRS director Frans Tijink told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said that despite some rain last weekend, drilling in the fields was progressing at a good rate. The sugar beet area would be around 115,000 hectares, close to last season's total.</p>
<p>The institute would be issuing its first computer-generated beet forecast in early August, he added. --Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
